---
code: cli-file-unreadable
envelope: invocation
when-fires: an input file failed to read for a reason outside the two named arms. cli/lib.rs humane_read_error, residual arm. {kind}, {path}, and PASSTHROUGH {detail}.
why: the residual arm passes the platforms own words through, because there is nothing more useful to say about an unclassed OS error than to quote it - and inventing a category would mis-attribute.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-file-unreadable && mise run loom:promote -- cli-file-unreadable`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-file-unreadable` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=webhost.sh
dorc: error[cli-file-unreadable]: sm cannot read results `probe-results.txt`: Is
a directory (os error 21)
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [-o <oracle.sh>]... [--debug-argv]
